   $q$Which evidence supports the reason that shade trees would reduce heat?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Tree roots soak up rainwater, which helps to reduce flooding on streets.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"mismatched-reason"},{"text":"Shade could lower cooling costs for Hollis Street apartments by 15 percent.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"mismatched-reason"},{"text":"Many people find that streets with trees are more pleasant for walking.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"mismatched-reason"},{"text":"Sidewalks averaged 128 degrees on Hollis Street and 94 degrees on Elm Row.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Sidewalks averaged 128 degrees on Hollis Street and 94 degrees on Elm Row.$q$, $q$The temperature measurements appear in the paragraph that begins "The strongest reason is heat." The 15 percent estimate supports the separate reason about saving money.$q$, 'draft', 'dfdebb9f-0616-5c80-8dec-1521c2f8d0a5')
