   $q$Why does the author mention that the students used the same thermometer and measured at the same time each day?$q$, $q$[{"text":"To explain why Hollis Street has dark pavement and very few trees.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-cause-effect"},{"text":"To show that the students were more careful than the city's energy office.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"To prove that trees would cool Hollis Street as soon as they are planted.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"To show that the comparison between the two streets was fair and reliable.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$To show that the comparison between the two streets was fair and reliable.$q$, $q$Using the same tool at the same time rules out some other reasons the readings might differ, which makes the evidence more trustworthy. The author actually admits trees will not cool the street "overnight."$q$, 'draft', 'dfdebb9f-0616-5c80-8dec-1521c2f8d0a5')
