   $q$How does the energy office report help the author answer residents' concerns about cost?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It proves that the roots of new trees will never crack the sidewalks on the street.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"mismatched-reason"},{"text":"It suggests that savings from cooler buildings could help balance the cost of trees.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It shows that the city could plant and care for the new trees at no cost at all.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overstates-evidence"},{"text":"It shows that Hollis Street is much hotter in July than nearby Elm Row is.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"mismatched-reason"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It suggests that savings from cooler buildings could help balance the cost of trees.$q$, $q$The author says "the energy savings would help balance the cost over time," which relies on the report's 15 percent estimate. The author admits the costs are "real," so the report does not show the trees are free.$q$, 'draft', 'dfdebb9f-0616-5c80-8dec-1521c2f8d0a5')
